## 3. What are the four Reactive Streams interfaces?

The Reactive Streams specification defines four interfaces.

### 1. Publisher<T>

A Publisher produces data and sends it to subscribers according to their requested demand.

```java
Publisher<String> publisher;
```

### 2. Subscriber<T>

A Subscriber receives data and lifecycle signals.

It defines four methods:

```java
void onSubscribe(Subscription subscription);

void onNext(T item);

void onError(Throwable throwable);

void onComplete();
```

### 3. Subscription

A Subscription connects a Publisher and a Subscriber.

It provides two methods:

```java
void request(long n);

void cancel();
```

`request(n)` tells the Publisher that the Subscriber is ready to receive up to `n` additional elements.

`cancel()` cancels the subscription.

### 4. Processor<T, R>

A Processor acts as both a Subscriber and a Publisher.

It can receive elements, transform or process them, and publish results downstream.

### Sequence of signals

```text
Subscriber                 Publisher
    |                          |
    |------ subscribe() ------>|
    |                          |
    |<----- onSubscribe() -----|
    |                          |
    |------ request(2) ------->|
    |                          |
    |<-------- onNext(A) ------|
    |<-------- onNext(B) ------|
    |                          |
    |------ request(1) ------->|
    |                          |
    |<-------- onNext(C) ------|
    |                          |
    |<------ onComplete() -----|
```

A Publisher may send zero or more `onNext` signals, followed by either `onComplete` or `onError`.

Only one terminal signal is allowed.

### Role of request(n)

`request(n)` implements backpressure.

It prevents a Publisher from overwhelming a slower Subscriber by allowing the Subscriber to control how many items it is prepared to receive.

**Conclusion:** The four interfaces are Publisher, Subscriber, Subscription, and Processor. The `request(n)` mechanism allows consumers to control demand and is central to Reactive Streams backpressure.

